{"id":"de1f753f3822fd5c","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.11.0, conversion builtins including @intToPtr and @ptrToInt were renamed to @ptrFromInt and @intFromPtr, respectively; @intToEnum and @enumToInt became @enumFromInt and @intFromEnum.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:23:33.716564281Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"a274c502c1c11a6b","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"@bitCast was not renamed in Zig 0.11.0; it remains @bitCast.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:23:33.716564281Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"b287283aa6f42f01","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 provides `@memcpy(dest, source)` and `@memset(dest, value)`; `@memcpy` can replace `std.mem.copy` for copying between non-overlapping slices (and when both operands are slices, they must have equal lengths), while the standard-library function was renamed `std.mem.copyForwards` for ordered copying where slices may overlap.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:23:45.80852151Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"867ef5bfe70b668b","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 changes overflow arithmetic builtins such as `@addWithOverflow` to return a tuple containing the wrapped result and an overflow indicator; for example, `const result, const overflow = @addWithOverflow(a, b);`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:23:51.112548789Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"5082a10c8b8d228e","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 adds tuple type declarations using struct declaration syntax without field types, for example `const T = struct { u32, u32 };`; it does not add tuple destructuring declarations such as `const a, const b = tuple;`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:23:58.297137569Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"c1beccccdb9e048f","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.11.0, the existing `@min` and `@max` builtins were changed to accept arbitrarily many arguments and to refine the result type for integers (and vectors of integers) using comptime-known bounds; they can be used with comptime-known or runtime values.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:24:12.902904072Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"d973ba6b0a4870bb","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.11.0, `@intFromBool` always returns the one-bit integer type `u1`; for example, `@intFromBool(true)` has type `u1`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:24:18.67808528Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"d065b0ce6e3b0c28","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.11.0, `std.json.parse`/`parseFree` were replaced by allocator-taking `std.json.parseFromSlice` and related `parseFrom*` APIs, whose non-Leaky variants return `std.json.Parsed(T)` and release parsed allocations with `Parsed(T).deinit()`; the `parseFrom*Leaky` variants are an exception and require the caller to manage an arena.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:24:26.89876784Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"a565dfb8650c13b5","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 makes the Zig Build System non-experimental and introduces package management through `build.zig.zon` dependency declarations.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:24:33.493216877Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"d1525b3fd44d67e0","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 changes `std.Build.addTest` to create a test artifact without running it; a build script must add a run step to execute the tests.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:24:38.679711344Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"00aa166e61801dd9","subject":"zig","time":"2024-04-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.12.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.12.0 rejects a local `var` that is never mutated; declare an immutable local with `const`, as in `const value = 42;`, instead.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.12.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:24:48.670489078Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"e3b380db6f3ea7e8","subject":"zig","time":"2024-04-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.12.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.12.0 adds destructuring for indexable aggregates—tuples, vectors, and arrays—using a comma-separated sequence of lvalues or local variable declarations on the left-hand side; for example, `const a, const b = value;` destructures the aggregate into two bindings.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.12.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:24:58.129754713Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"2878ac578c988852","subject":"zig","time":"2024-04-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.12.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.12.0 renames `std.os` to `std.posix` for POSIX operating-system APIs; code using those APIs imports `std.posix`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.12.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:25:02.962762483Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"1391c8e2c096501c","subject":"zig","time":"2024-04-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.12.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.12.0 makes build dependencies lazy: build scripts use `b.lazyDependency(...)` to request a dependency conditionally, and `build.zig.zon` declares dependencies as lazy when they need not be fetched for every build.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.12.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:25:08.516063656Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"db79e86bdfce340c","subject":"zig","time":"2024-06-07T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.13.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.13.0 renames `std.ComptimeStringMap` to `std.StaticStringMap`; the new map initializer accepts a single compile-time list of key-value pairs, for example `std.StaticStringMap(u8).initComptime(.{ .{\"a\", 1}, .{\"b\", 2} })`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.13.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:25:14.881814057Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"7b6ce630aabc42d7","subject":"zig","time":"2024-06-07T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.13.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.13.0, `std.ChildProcess` was renamed to `std.process.Child`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.13.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:25:21.761404531Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"379aab4dfe346f78","subject":"zig","time":"2024-06-07T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.13.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.13.0, some other functions were also moved from `std.ChildProcess` to the `std.process` namespace.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.13.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:25:21.761404531Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"40fa5195f0d32149","subject":"zig","time":"2024-06-07T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.13.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.13.0 adds ZIP archive support in `std.zip` and allows a package to declare a ZIP URL as its source in `build.zig.zon`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.13.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:25:31.444925657Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"303256d45b1f8957","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 adds labeled switch expressions/statements, allowing a switch to be targeted by `break`; for example, `const result = sw: switch (x) { 0 =\u003e break :sw 10, else =\u003e 20 };`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:25:45.133992589Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"4cf64577db4ce470","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.14.0, a container type cannot have a field and a declaration (`const`, `var`, or `fn`) with the same name within that container; this does not prohibit a top-level declaration from sharing its name with a field of the type it defines, so `const Thing = struct { Thing: u32 };` is not barred by this restriction.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:25:53.363290277Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"8a05eaac75bcf7d1","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 expands `@splat` to support arrays as well as vectors; for example, `const a: [4]u8 = @splat(0);`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:26:02.136320944Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"e7b03fb880d83d2c","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 changes `@export` to take a pointer to the value being exported, for example `@export(\u0026function, .{ .name = \"function\" });`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:26:18.244003432Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"9b01a6d23e493a07","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 replaces `@setCold` with `@branchHint`; `@branchHint(.unlikely);` hints that control flow reaches the enclosing block rarely, and must be the first statement in that block (for example, the body of an `if`).","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:26:25.028952512Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"01d61a7b9995a6e5","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 removes `@fence`; the release notes say to replace its effects by strengthening the relevant atomic memory orderings or adding atomic operations. The required operation depends on the synchronization pattern; a load/store with an explicit memory order is not a general replacement, and some cases require read-modify-write operations or an additional atomic variable.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:26:31.013506972Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"5e4f667abe033d1c","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 removes anonymous struct types and unifies tuple syntax with struct literals; tuple-like values use `.{ ... }`, for example `const pair = .{ 1, \"x\" };`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:26:42.793938396Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"80345ab757925f91","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 adds `@FieldType(Container, \"field\")` to obtain a named field's type; for example, `const T = @FieldType(MyStruct, \"value\");`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:26:53.950228846Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"52cd0cae93a1b86f","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 disallows non-scalar sentinel values for pointers, arrays, and slices; a sentinel must be a scalar value such as `0` for `[:0]const u8`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:27:02.035519134Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"798c4a449bc94606","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 added `std.mem.Allocator.remap` (and `Allocator.VTable.remap`), which attempts to resize an allocation while allowing relocation; a null result means the resize could not be done without the caller performing an allocate-copy-free operation.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:27:14.486398762Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"7e2ec3e1ee28b124","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.14.0, `std.mem.Allocator.resize` continues to report success or failure with a `bool` and guarantees not to move the pointer; the release did not change its semantics.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:27:14.486398762Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"10855018784f26e2","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 changes `std.ArrayList` and related containers toward unmanaged-style APIs: a list no longer stores its allocator, so operations that allocate take an allocator argument.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:27:20.789887755Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"44daf327491997b0","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 introduces a new package hash format, which includes package name, version, fingerprint ID component, and total unpacked size alongside 200 bits of SHA-256.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:27:27.753637115Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"61e14b2cfd5fb449","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 continues to support the legacy package-hash format; its release notes do not state that package managers automatically regenerate outdated hashes.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:27:27.753637115Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"1c5bf762856f7303","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 removes `usingnamespace`; declarations must be imported or explicitly re-exported instead, for example `pub const Foo = other.Foo;`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:27:34.404736121Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"f2b7ad962fc3c5ea","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 removes the `async` and `await` keywords and the language's async/await function-call syntax.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:27:47.518515519Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ec1fa5392ccccbd9","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 changes formatted printing so types with a `format` method are formatted using the `{f}` specifier, for example `try writer.print(\"{f}\", .{value});`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:27:59.308851593Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"32aaeba1d2129c90","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 requires custom `format` methods to use the writer-based signature without a format-string or options parameter; formatted printing no longer implicitly calls those methods with `{}`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:28:09.047423412Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"7dbd9197a4e52e17","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 makes `std.ArrayList` unmanaged by default, so list operations that allocate require an allocator argument; for example, use `try list.append(allocator, item);`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:28:17.537798348Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"cd4e6b2bc787075f","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 removes `std.BoundedArray`; fixed-capacity collections must use another container or an explicitly managed array and length.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:28:29.285031955Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"753a899586914f14","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 deletes the old `std.io.bufferedWriter` abstraction; the new `std.Io.Writer` has its buffer in the interface, so a separate `BufferedWriter` abstraction is no longer needed.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:28:39.551716995Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"37325817747dd2b1","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 deletes `CountingWriter`; the release notes recommend `std.Io.Writer.Discarding`, `std.Io.Writer.Allocating`, or `std.Io.Writer.fixed` for the corresponding use cases, and advise against adding a stream-graph node solely to count bytes.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:28:39.551716995Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"705716674b7c7af4","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 makes formatted-printing alignment ASCII/byte-based rather than Unicode-codepoint-aware; the prior implementation was not fully Unicode-aware, and the standard library does not provide the full Unicode support needed to align Unicode strings.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:28:52.737921684Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"0c29679d53a6edd5","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 removes the deprecated implicit root module from the build API; build scripts must explicitly provide or create the root module when adding compilation artifacts.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:29:07.032105804Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"f20a9ce7208f850e","subject":"zig","time":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.16.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.16.0, `@cImport` is deprecated, and the release notes provide a build-system translation workflow that imports the generated module; however, `@cImport` remains available in this release, so projects are not yet required to switch.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.16.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:29:16.352761903Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"bce5fedd268975e9","subject":"zig","time":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.16.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.16.0 replaces the reflective `@Type` constructor with dedicated type-creating builtins such as `@Int`, `@Pointer`, `@Struct`, `@Union`, and `@Enum`; for example, use `@Int(.unsigned, 32)` to construct `u32`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.16.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:29:21.083713278Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"28a0808ee50abd55","subject":"zig","time":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.16.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.16.0 introduces `std.Io` as an explicit I/O interface: operations requiring I/O receive an `Io` value rather than relying on implicit global I/O state.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.16.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:29:27.493774755Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"fb67a25128c3e086","subject":"zig","time":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.16.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.16.0 removes `std.Thread.Pool`; code using the standard library thread pool must migrate to another concurrency mechanism.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.16.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:29:33.449090584Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"94be594b76e5b2fe","subject":"zig","time":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.16.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.16.0, `Io.File.Stat.atime` is optional because access times may be unavailable; callers can handle `null` with `stat.atime orelse return error.FileAccessTimeUnavailable`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.16.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:29:38.657853507Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"b8b3abada6d994ad","subject":"zig","time":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.16.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.16.0 removes most functions from `std.posix` and `std.os.windows`, not the namespaces themselves; for removed functions, the release notes direct users either to higher-level `std.Io` interfaces or lower-level `std.posix.system` calls.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.16.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:29:51.14485143Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"6119d5db08a802ea","subject":"zig","time":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.16.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.16.0, `std.Io.Writer` and `std.Io.Reader` replace the generic `std.io.GenericReader`, `std.io.GenericWriter`, `std.io.AnyReader`, and `std.io.FixedBufferStream` APIs.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.16.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:29:58.477298294Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ee6d12c89e832571","subject":"zig","time":"2026-10-01T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.17.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.17.0 changes `@bitCast` to reinterpret the logical bit representation of its operand, independent of physical memory layout; for example, bitcasting a byte array to an integer uses the language-defined logical bit ordering.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:30:09.183019355Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"3453788b83da94f1","subject":"zig","time":"2026-10-01T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.17.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.17.0 removes array multiplication syntax such as `[_]u8{0} ** 4`; use an explicit array initializer or `@splat` instead, for example `const values: [4]u8 = @splat(0);`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:30:19.409285131Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"7b5b66e8ad31ea88","subject":"zig","time":"2026-10-01T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.17.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.17.0 adds `@divCeil(numerator, denominator)` for integer division rounded toward positive infinity; for example, `@divCeil(5, 2)` evaluates to `3`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:30:31.964878293Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"e01780e856ce0f50","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"In Zig 0.15.1, an integer-to-float coercion is a compile error at comptime when the integer cannot be represented precisely by the target float; the release notes show changing the integer literal to a floating-point literal to opt into rounding. The claim is too broad in saying lossy implicit coercion is generally disallowed and that `@floatFromInt` is the prescribed workaround.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:30:51.787368302Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"3213dab77b090fe5","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 allows additional boolean vector operations, including bitwise not, and, or, xor, and boolean not.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:31:05.228988723Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"b91d6e22acf6cc78","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 requires typed inline-assembly clobbers instead of string clobber names, expressing clobbers through the assembly constraint type rather than an untyped string.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:31:20.192553063Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"1cabec948a1cde79","subject":"zig","time":"2024-04-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.12.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.12.0 makes `@fieldParentPtr` infer the result pointer type from its result location, so a call supplies the field name, field pointer, and parent type, for example `const parent: *Parent = @fieldParentPtr(\"child\", child_ptr);`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.12.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:31:32.778641025Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"6ef3676a4575a75f","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 introduces `@inComptime()` to determine whether the current code is being evaluated at compile time; for example, `if (@inComptime()) { ... }`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:31:41.695158122Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"30159c31f585bc4e","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 replaces `@qualCast` with separate `@constCast` and `@volatileCast` builtins; for example, `@constCast(ptr)` removes const qualification while preserving the pointer type.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:31:48.26299797Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"277fbb8553191c93","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 changes function calls made from comptime to be analyzed only at comptime, rather than also requiring runtime-valid analysis.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:31:58.828898418Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"82daf09dff95e7ec","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 changes `@typeInfo` so that it does not expose private declarations of a type; reflection through `@typeInfo` sees only public declarations.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:32:12.19238919Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"b3612a491172b962","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 forbids a source file from belonging to multiple modules in one compilation; shared code must be provided through a single module dependency.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:32:21.735343764Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"fc88a7f39b6df5c3","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 permits a `for` loop to iterate over multiple sequences in parallel, for example `for (items, indices) |item, index| { ... }`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:32:27.371332463Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"be6903f3d0cc0c9c","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 allows indexing pointers to tuples and vectors; for example, a pointer to a tuple can be indexed as `tuple_ptr[0]`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:32:35.162925943Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"d7d4e8eccc3b54f0","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"In Zig 0.11.0, `std.mem.span` and `std.mem.len` reject ordinary many-item pointers that lack a sentinel, so a sentinel-terminated pointer such as `[*:0]const u8` is needed for those pointers. They also accept `[*c]` C pointers, which these functions assume are non-null and zero-terminated.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:32:53.280481684Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"0622229ca6627a13","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 adds `std.heap.wasm_allocator`, a WebAssembly-specific allocator that permits memory shrink operations to fail.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:33:02.732373526Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ac74c5d2bc6b22bc","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 adds `std.meta.FieldType`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:33:10.378339173Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"f0152cf4212c77e6","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0 retains `std.meta.FieldEnum` and fixes its handling of empty structs.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:33:10.378339173Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ce729a344f72fc59","subject":"zig","time":"2023-08-04T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.11.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.11.0's release notes list `std.meta.isTag` and `std.meta.tagName` as removed; the standard-library source retains deprecated declarations for them that produce compile errors.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.11.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:33:10.378339173Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"0a1ca312f7e68617","subject":"zig","time":"2024-04-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.12.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.12.0 changes HTTP server APIs substantially: `std.http.Headers` is removed and the previous server API is replaced by a redesigned server interface.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.12.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:33:21.341148594Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"309901d485313038","subject":"zig","time":"2024-04-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.12.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.12.0 makes POSIX API arguments more type-safe, including using typed file descriptors and typed flags rather than unstructured integers.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.12.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:33:29.944254171Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"84438cd200b9e687","subject":"zig","time":"2024-04-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.12.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.12.0 adds system package mode to the build system, allowing build options to require installed system libraries and avoiding network dependency fetching in that mode.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.12.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:33:45.82221959Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"52b254e4e45c4818","subject":"zig","time":"2024-04-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.12.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.12.0 adds `b.path(...)` for constructing paths relative to the build root and deprecates `LazyPath.relative`.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.12.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:33:58.813454236Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"720914d41ee224ac","subject":"zig","time":"2024-06-07T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.13.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.13.0 changes `std.PriorityQueue` to store only its valid items in the `items` field and to track allocated capacity separately; accessing `items` no longer exposes uninitialized capacity.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.13.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:34:04.958152142Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"58f794206af1b24a","subject":"zig","time":"2024-06-07T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.13.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.13.0 reworked CLI progress reporting around `std.Progress`: the caller starts a root node, then attaches a child process's progress subtree by setting `child.progress_node` to the appropriate node before spawning it. The API does not require that the root progress node itself be passed to every child process.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.13.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:34:11.592860897Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"8d294d491af705f1","subject":"zig","time":"2024-06-07T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.13.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.13.0 installs Windows DLL artifacts to `\u003cprefix\u003e/bin/` by default, alongside executables.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.13.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:34:21.673203861Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"c2ee2ca77022deef","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 adds file-system watching facilities to the build system, allowing build steps to watch directories and rerun when inputs change.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:34:34.183327283Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"021c79742f096d0f","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 adds `std.hash_map` rehash support through a `rehash` method.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:34:51.054751347Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"06b43b437ab7581d","subject":"zig","time":"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.14.0"},"statement":"Zig 0.14.0 adds ZON parsing and serialization APIs to the standard library, allowing ZON values to be parsed and emitted at runtime.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.14.0/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:34:55.509455191Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"a22eafbcf3824f32","subject":"zig","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.15.1"},"statement":"Zig 0.15.1 introduces `std.Io.Reader` and `std.Io.Writer` as non-generic I/O interfaces and deprecates existing `std.io` readers and writers in their favor; the older APIs are not stated to be removed, and an adapter is provided for old streams.","source":"https://ziglang.org/download/0.15.1/release-notes.html","added":"2026-10-25T21:30:42.625249524Z","by":"user"}
